. *==============================================================================
. * 3. CONTROLLING FOR INCOME
. *    Published: coupons +0.2673 (SE 0.1203, p 0.031); income +0.3836.
. *    The sign flips — a textbook Simpson's paradox.
. *==============================================================================
. regress sales coupons income

      Source |       SS           df       MS      Number of obs   =        50
-------------+----------------------------------   F(2, 47)        =     13.20
       Model |  275.780642         2  137.890321   Prob > F        =    0.0000
    Residual |    490.8118        47  10.4428043   R-squared       =    0.3597
-------------+----------------------------------   Adj R-squared   =    0.3325
       Total |  766.592442        49  15.6447437   Root MSE        =    3.2315

------------------------------------------------------------------------------
       sales | Coefficient  Std. err.      t    P>|t|     [95% conf. interval]
-------------+----------------------------------------------------------------
     coupons |   .2673097   .1202762     2.22   0.031     .0253452    .5092743
      income |   .3836135   .0764909     5.02   0.000     .2297336    .5374933
       _cons |   5.027757    7.18074     0.70   0.487    -9.418029    19.47354
------------------------------------------------------------------------------

. scalar b_full  = _b[coupons]

. scalar se_full = _se[coupons]

. scalar g_hat   = _b[income]

. show "Full slope (sales on coupons + income)" b_full
Full slope (sales on coupons + income)            0.2673

. show "  its SE" se_full
  its SE                                          0.1203

. show "Income coefficient, gamma_hat" g_hat
Income coefficient, gamma_hat                     0.3836

. 
